                <pb facs="0796" n="758" xml:id="pg758"/>

                <head>283. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>President Eisenhower, accompanied by Prime Minister Macmillan, left the Mid-Ocean
                    Club at 10:10 a.m. on March 24 and drove to Kindley Air Force Base. The
                    President left Bermuda shortly after 10:30. (Eisenhower Library, President’s
                    Appointment Book) Prime Minister Macmillan remained in Bermuda another 3 days.
                    On March 25 and 26, he had conversations with Canadian Prime Minister Louis St.
                    Laurent and Foreign Minister Lester B. Pearson. (Harold Macmillan, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Riding the Storm,</hi> page 258)</p>
            </div>
